 "answer": "On a GPU with 32 GiB of VRAM, Ollama's default context length should be **32k tokens (32,768)**. Recent Ollama versions pick the default from available VRAM, roughly:\n\n- Under 24 GiB: 4k\n- 24 to 48 GiB: 32k\n- 48 GiB or more: 256k\n\nI'm not certain of the exact thresholds or when they were introduced, so check the release notes for your installed version. You can override the default with the `OLLAMA_CONTEXT_LENGTH` environment variable or the `num_ctx` parameter in a request or Modelfile.",
